# DTF tier manifest: scan-on-proxy-conda-and-content  (artifact-keeper 1.11.0:
# #4585 conda scan-on-proxy gate, #4041 build-qualified conda purls, #4042 /
# #4088 / #4089 conda -> PyPI identity, #4058 conda policy predicates, #4556
# passed predicates in promotion gate_results, #4516 admin hold queues)
# Profile-set: filesystem + upstreams.mock-conda-scan (a stdlib http.server
# conda channel the oracle fills with host-built packages via docker cp; the
# builder is harness/tiers/conda-proxy-scan-grading/fixtures/build_pkg.py).
# LOCAL-ONLY: verdicts come from the backend image's bundled Grype and its
# pre-seeded vulnerability DB; no scanner sidecar, no OSV, no internet. No
# package this tier scans names a dependency, and none of them maps to a PyPI
# distribution the dependency scanner would ask OSV about.
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS
# #4585  before 1.11.0 a conda Remote with scan_on_proxy streamed every
#        package unscanned. Now .conda/.tar.bz2 downloads run the inline gate
#        (vulnerable 403 scan_blocked, clean X-AK-Scan: clean, an identity the
#        package's own index.json does not back 423 under fail_closed), on the
#        plain route, both /t/<token>/ forms and through a Virtual; a blocked
#        package's .sigs sidecar is refused; the generic download route refuses
#        proxied conda files (403 scan_on_proxy_route_required); GET
#        /api/v1/formats says conda and conda_native are `enforced`.
# #4041  a conda artifact's stored identity purl, and its own scan-inventory
#        row, name the build: pkg:conda/<n>@<v>?build=..&channel=..&subdir=..
#        (two subdir builds, two purls; noarch stays subdir=noarch).
# #4042/#4088/#4089  the identity records the PyPI alias (py-opencv ->
#        opencv-python) or that PyPI advisories were NOT queried (unmapped).
# #4058  scan-policy predicates.conda.denied_licenses blocks the download of a
#        hosted package declaring that license (quarantined with a
#        [conda.license] reason); #4556 a promotion under the same predicate
#        lists the passed policy-predicate in gate_results.
# #4516  GET /api/v1/admin/holds/{summary,quarantine} list that hold; a
#        repository-scoped admin token is refused.
#
# Red: ak-backend:1.10.0. Green: ak-backend:1.11.0 and newer.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: admin setup plus ~40 calls back to back.
# UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true: the mock sits on a private per-slot subnet.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-conda-scan"
